#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# discrete_wavelet_data

#% text
# `discrete_wavelet_data(coefficients, info)` holds the result of a discrete wavelet transform. `d(all)` gives every coefficient array as index -> array, `d(automatic)` the arrays of the leaves (which determine the data), `d(index)` or `d(pattern)` the selected ones, and `d(property)` the properties "Wavelet", "Levels", "Transform", "Padding", "DataDimensions", "BasisIndex" (`d("Properties")` lists them).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
d = discrete_wavelet_transform(n(range(8)), haar_wavelet(), 3)

#% cell
d("BasisIndex")
#% output
#= [[1], [0, 1], [0, 0, 0], [0, 0, 1]]

#% cell
d([0, _])
#% output
#= [[0, 0] -> [5.000000000000001, 13.000000000000002], [0, 1] -> [-2.000000000000001, -2.0]]

#% cell
d("Levels")
#% output
#= 3

